# Branch policy (hard)

This repository has **exactly two branches**: `main` and `dev`. Never create another branch — not with `git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, GitHub, a worktree, a cloud agent, or a PR workflow.

## Work only on `dev`

1. `git checkout dev` and `git pull --ff-only origin dev`.
2. Commit and `git push origin dev` on that branch.
3. A push to `dev` deploys to https://dev.rive.work.

Do not open a feature PR. There is no third branch to PR from.

## `main` is production, merge-only

- Never commit, push, force-push, amend, or cherry-pick onto `main`.
- The only update path is a **merge commit** PR: `dev` → `main`, after `dev.rive.work` is good.
- `git push origin main` is forbidden even when the tree looks correct.

## If you are not on `dev`

Check out `dev` and continue there. Do not branch off to "keep main clean" — `dev` is that gate.
